---
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import SignupForm from '../components/SignupForm.astro';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="TachyonCMS · fast for the developer, easy for the editor" path="/">
  <PageHero
    title="Fast for the developer. Easy for the editor. No plugins holding it together."
    lede="TachyonCMS is an open-source CMS written in Rust, and we're building it in public."
  />
  <div class="intro">
    <p>
      Pick a CMS today and you usually pick a side. One kind is a joy to code against and baffling to whoever
      publishes the Tuesday newsletter. The other is easy to publish with, and you pay for that in plugins, patches
      and page speed.
    </p>
    <p>
      We don't think you should have to choose. The core already runs on Postgres. Your content types live in a file
      you can review like code, and when something's wrong the API names the exact field. The editor's side comes
      next. And speed? We'll publish the benchmarks before we quote you a single number.
    </p>
  </div>
  <SignupForm source="home" />
</Base>

<style>
  .intro {
    max-width: 40rem;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    color: var(--c-muted);
  }
</style>
